Package: ReproducibleCDI
Title: Reproducing the Community Deprivation Index of Neighborhood Socioeconomic Status
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Rafael", "Catoia Pulgrossi", email = "rcatoiap@stanford.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Tae Yoon", "Lee", email = "harrytyl@stanford.edu", role = c("aut")))
Description: Provides a simple, tidy interface for calculating the Community
    Deprivation Index (CDI), a composite measure of neighborhood-level
    socioeconomic deprivation, using data from the US Census Bureau's American
    Community Survey (ACS). The CDI follows the Singh/Area Deprivation Index
    (ADI) methodology - a principal-component-weighted composite of 18
    standardized ACS variables computed natively at the census block group
    level - and adds a percentage-uninsured variable. Features include
    automatic data fetching, flexible geographies (county, tract, block group),
    principal component analysis, hierarchical (block group -> tract -> county)
    imputation, and rescaling to a 1-100 percentile ranking.
